WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.842
Welcome to the STEM Production Tracker,

00:00:02.842 --> 00:00:06.092
the system that replaces the STEM Status spreadsheet.

00:00:06.092 --> 00:00:11.121
In the next three minutes, we'll walk through the dashboard, orders, the pipeline,

00:00:11.121 --> 00:00:13.513
the knowledgebase, and the admin tools.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.648
You sign in with your work email.

00:00:16.648 --> 00:00:20.523
The first time, your administrator gives you a temporary password,

00:00:20.523 --> 00:00:24.046
and the app asks you to choose your own before you continue.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.296
The dashboard opens first.

00:00:27.296 --> 00:00:31.783
It follows the same sections as the old 2026 Story sheet,

00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.695
but now every colour means one thing.

00:00:34.695 --> 00:00:36.820
Green is done, or money in.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.395
Blue is in progress.

00:00:38.395 --> 00:00:39.890
Amber needs action.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.071
Red is at risk.

00:00:41.071 --> 00:00:44.219
And purple is forecast, not yet on a PO.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.885
Section one shows how the year can land.

00:00:47.885 --> 00:00:51.151
Committed is everything shipped, plus orders on a PO.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:54.603
Pipeline and Awaiting PO come from the new Pipeline tab,

00:00:54.603 --> 00:00:57.006
and Total Projected adds them together.

00:00:57.006 --> 00:01:00.704
The bar underneath tracks progress against the revenue goal.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:07.345
Section two shows what's shipped, and the cash behind it: shipped, billed, paid,

00:01:07.345 --> 00:01:08.298
and collected.

00:01:08.298 --> 00:01:12.178
An amber card, like Shipped, Not Billed, is a to-do list.

00:01:12.178 --> 00:01:14.628
When it reaches zero, it turns grey.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:19.358
Section three covers orders on a PO that haven't shipped yet.

00:01:19.358 --> 00:01:21.961
Anything without a bill month shows in amber,

00:01:21.961 --> 00:01:25.085
and at-risk orders are kept out of the totals, in red.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.661
On the Orders tab, each row is coloured by where the order stands:

00:01:30.661 --> 00:01:34.577
green for shipped, blue when devices are still outstanding,

00:01:34.577 --> 00:01:39.290
yellow when it's scheduled or in build, and grey for next year's queue.

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.878
Search by school or sales order number.

00:01:41.878 --> 00:01:46.392
Non-lab orders, like SnappyXO, appear when you tick Show All Orders.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:49.370
Click an order to open it.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:52.861
Order details come from NetSuite every ten minutes.

00:01:52.861 --> 00:01:58.337
Your team fills in the rest: device POs, ship and install dates, billing status,

00:01:58.337 --> 00:01:59.022
and notes.

00:01:59.022 --> 00:02:03.129
You can only change the fields your role is responsible for.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:09.505
The Pipeline tab is where Sales tracks opportunities that aren't on a PO yet.

00:02:09.505 --> 00:02:14.883
Each one has a stage, a likelihood, an estimated value, and an expected PO date.

00:02:14.883 --> 00:02:17.638
The year's revenue goal is set here, too.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.637
To enter many at once, download the Excel template, fill it in, and upload it.

00:02:23.637 --> 00:02:28.434
You'll see a preview of what will be added or updated before anything changes.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:33.600
Totals are saved every Monday, so the dashboard can show the change since last week.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.171
Everything is documented in the Knowledgebase: a quickstart guide,

00:02:39.171 --> 00:02:41.952
a full instruction manual, and this video.

00:02:41.952 --> 00:02:45.065
Each article can be printed, or saved as a PDF.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.737
Administrators also get an Admin tab.

00:02:48.737 --> 00:02:53.958
Here you can add users with a temporary password, edit their details and role,

00:02:53.958 --> 00:02:57.372
reset passwords, and suspend access with one click.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:03.717
The audit trail records everything: every change, with its old and new value,

00:03:03.717 --> 00:03:08.597
who made it, and when, plus sign-ins, user changes, and NetSuite updates.

00:03:08.597 --> 00:03:10.936
Entries can't be edited or deleted.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:17.286
And the backup page downloads a complete copy of the system, as an Excel workbook,

00:03:17.286 --> 00:03:19.733
and an exact JSON file for safekeeping.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.032
That's the tour.

00:03:22.032 --> 00:03:26.649
For more detail, open the Knowledgebase, or ask your administrator.

00:03:26.649 --> 00:03:28.027
Thanks for watching.
